exports[`each template's output > allowance_fallback, for clients: the snapshot 1`] = `
{
  "html": "<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark">
<title>Allowance used: calls go to your direct line until 6 November</title>
<style>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body, .hd-wrap { background: #0d1117 !important; color: #e6edf3 !important; }
  .hd-muted { color: #9da7b3 !important; }
  a { color: #8cc4ff !important; }
  a.hd-action { background: #e6edf3 !important; color: #0d1117 !important; }
}</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;color:#1f2328;">
<span style="display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;mso-hide:all;">You chose “Stop and fall back” for when your allowance runs out.</span>
<div class="hd-wrap" style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px;font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#1f2328;background:#ffffff;">
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">All 1,000 voice minutes in your plan are used for this period. You chose “Stop and fall back” for when that happens, so until Friday 6 November, when your allowance resets, AYA doesn&#39;t answer new calls: they go to your direct line instead. A call she&#39;s already on carries on.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">To keep AYA answering instead, switch to “Keep going and bill the extra” in Billing. Usage past the allowance is then billed for each started block of 100 voice minutes at your plan&#39;s overage rates, which are provisional until we&#39;ve measured our costs.</p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 24px;"><a class="hd-action" href="https://app.healdesk.test/" style="display:inline-block;background:#1f2328;color:#ffffff;padding:10px 16px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Change it in Billing</a></p>
<hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;margin:24px 0 16px;">
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">You&#39;re receiving this because this is the address on Radiance Med Spa&#39;s healdesk account.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out patient details.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">healdesk is a service of Viixi FZC, a company registered under the Sharjah Publishing City Free Zone, United Arab Emirates.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">US mailing address (correspondence only): 800 N King Street, Suite 304-1426, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>",
  "preheader": "You chose “Stop and fall back” for when your allowance runs out.",
  "subject": "Allowance used: calls go to your direct line until 6 November",
  "text": "All 1,000 voice minutes in your plan are used for this period. You chose “Stop and fall back” for when that happens, so until Friday 6 November, when your allowance resets, AYA doesn't answer new calls: they go to your direct line instead. A call she's already on carries on.

To keep AYA answering instead, switch to “Keep going and bill the extra” in Billing. Usage past the allowance is then billed for each started block of 100 voice minutes at your plan's overage rates, which are provisional until we've measured our costs.

Change it in Billing: https://app.healdesk.test/

